      "writtenOn": "2022-03-31T21:10:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You generally shouldn\u0027t be type asserting to a concrete type, use an interface instead.  That becomes especially important if somebody wraps another type around apex.Prebuilt.\n\nThe new, bazel-like pattern is to use ctx.SetProvider in the modules that export the relevant information, and then use ctx.ModuleHasProvider and ctx.ModuleProvider to access it here.",
      "revId": "f6642fafe27a9a5d33ea42fe8818c3225eaee606",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19362bfe_d1bc8754",
